{# gfadmin/templates/admin/form.html rendered with a NeedForm (givefood/
   forms.py:231-236) -- the edit half of Django's one need_form view.
   admin/need_new.njk in this same directory is the create half; field
   NAMES, ids and labels are kept identical between the two (see that
   file's own header comment for the WP 6.8 note on merging them).

   FIXES admin/form.html:8-10's column-is-half bug (defect class already
   named in generic_form.njk's own header comment): Bulma's
   `.column.is-half` is a hard 50% whether or not a sibling column exists,
   so pinning it drew every need with no matching preview (most needs --
   see the `show_proxy` gate below) as a half-width strip with an empty
   right half. Two bare `.column`s still split 50/50, so the preview case
   is unchanged. #}
{% extends "admin/page.njk" %}

{% block title %}Edit Need{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column">
    <h2>Edit Need</h2>
{# NO BACK LINK. Every admin form in this port used to carry a
   "&larr; Back" above the fields; Django's own admin has none anywhere
   (`grep -rn "&larr;" gfadmin/templates/admin/*.html` is empty), so these
   were a port addition. Removed 2026-09-05, maintainer decision -- the
   navbar and the browser both already go back, and a link that leaves an
   edit form is worth less than the row it occupies. #}

    {# Django shows per-field errors inline (`{{ form|bulma }}`); this port
       validates in the route and surfaces the first failure as one banner,
       matching admin/need_new.njk:35-37 and generic_form.njk:27. #}
    {% if error %}<div class="notification is-danger is-light">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}

    <form method="post" class="form-edit-need">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

      {# NO FOOD BANK FIELD. Django's NeedForm (givefood/forms.py:232)
         exposes `foodbank` as an editable ModelChoiceField and this port
         carried that over as a slug input; it was made read-only earlier on
         2026-09-05, then removed outright -- a need is created against the
         food bank whose page produced it, the page's own title and Back link
         already say which one that is, and repeating it as a field the form
         cannot change is a label pretending to be an input.

         routes/admin/needs.ts keeps whatever foodbank_id the need already
         has. The create half (admin/need_new.njk) still picks one, because
         that is where the association is made. #}
      </div>

      {# Labels are the model's explicit verbose_names (givefood/models/needs.py:64
         "Shopping List" and :67 "Excess Items"), matching admin/need_new.njk:68-70.

         The two ids are load-bearing, not cosmetic: static/js/admin.js:103-104
         selects these textareas as `#id_change_text` / `#id_excess_change_text`
         and initChangeTextButtons() (admin.js:408-409) returns at its first
         line when the first is missing, so without them the "Make Titlecase",
         "CSV to Lines" and "Find & Replace" buttons are never injected on
         THIS form either -- the same defect need_new.njk already fixed on
         the create half.

         `required` matches needs.py:64: change_text has no blank=True, so
         NeedForm builds a required field. Server-side check in needs.ts's
         adminNeedEditForm. #}
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_change_text">Shopping List</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" id="id_change_text" name="change_text" rows="6" required>{{ need.change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
        <p class="help">One item per line.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_excess_change_text">Excess Items</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" id="id_excess_change_text" name="excess_change_text" rows="6">{{ need.excess_change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" name="published" value="1"{% if need.published %} checked{% endif %}> Published</label>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# admin/form.html:14/31's `onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;"`
         double-submit guard, on every Django admin submit button -- this
         one had been dropped. Without it, a slow save re-entered by a
         second click/Enter can race two writes (and, once published, two
         translate-job batches) against the same need. #}
      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <button type="submit" class="button is-link is-light" onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;">Submit</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>

  {# admin/form.html:23-29's `{% if need %}{% if need.uri %}...{% endif %}{% endif %}`
     preview column -- the page the shopping list was extracted from, not
     necessarily the food bank's current site. See needs.ts's
     computeNeedProxySrc for the field-based-proxy substitution (Django's
     raw `?url=` was the SSRF WP 6.3 already fixed everywhere else). #}
  {% if show_proxy %}
  <div class="column">
    <h3>Preview</h3>
    <iframe class="preview-frame" src="{{ proxy_src }}" style="width:100%;height:1000px;border:none;" loading="lazy"></iframe>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
